00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:53.586
Alrifht

00:10:53.586 --> 00:10:55.321
Ready to pour the floor

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:58.557
I have some assistance
because it needs to be done quite fast.

00:10:59.925 --> 00:11:02.928
It's a product that needs to be mixed quite thinly.

00:11:03.029 --> 00:11:05.431
So with a lot of water,
and then you pour it.

00:11:05.431 --> 00:11:08.100
And it will kind of self level

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:08.668
Here and there you help it bit

00:11:08.668 --> 00:11:11.671
and you measure it if it’s level.

00:11:12.505 --> 00:11:14.974
So we set up, an assembly line,

00:11:14.974 --> 00:11:18.210
I'm going to do all the mixing.
got a bucket with a hole in it.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:21.080
So just pour the water in there
and then it will drain itself.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:24.083
So you always have
the same amount of water for a mix.

00:11:24.984 --> 00:11:31.957
the time between the first
and the last mix needs to be as short as possible
because it cures quite quickly.

00:11:33.526 --> 00:11:37.463
And then generally what is done
is, with a spike roller,

00:11:37.963 --> 00:11:42.301
You roll the floor when it's still wet,
so air bubbles can rise up and go out.

00:11:43.235 --> 00:11:46.939
But I didn't find the right roller
because it needs to be quite deep,

00:11:47.273 --> 00:11:50.276
because at some point it's
going to be like 3cm thick

00:11:50.643 --> 00:11:53.813
and at the edges it’s thinner,
because the concrete floor is a bit

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.349
going like that, it  cups a bit.

00:11:57.349 --> 00:11:58.184
So I don't have that.

00:11:58.184 --> 00:12:01.287
So I'm not expecting perfection
on the first time we do this.

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:05.057
We'll see how that turns out.

